From 1d291c40301356437e91c3c65e6845de48d12e44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:02:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tools): bound the wait hint's card-show flag loop and say
 "bounded", not "linear" [daveey]

Review follow-up to #3533 (review 5950525933, non-blocking point 1). The module
called its scan linear, but _CARD_SHOW_RE was quadratic in repeated `kanban`
words: a flag's value can itself be the word `kanban`, so the unbounded flag
loop ran to the end of the text from every start. `"kanban --a " * 727`
(8,000 characters) took about 0.6 s on the reviewer's machine and about 70 ms
on an M-series Mac.

- _CARD_SHOW_RE reads at most MAX_CARD_SHOW_FLAGS (8) flags per `kanban` word;
  the same input now takes about 1.5 ms. `kanban [up to 8 flags] show <id>`
  still matches.
- Docstring and comments describe the work as bounded and say how.
- .env.example: TERMINAL_MAX_WAIT defaults to 400 or TERMINAL_TIMEOUT when that
  is larger, and is held under the per-call deadline only while it is on.
- website env-var reference: same correction about the deadline.
- test: the handler-path test scopes its temporary patches with
  monkeypatch.context() in place of monkeypatch.undo(), which also dropped the
  suite's hermetic fixtures for the rest of that test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
